{title: Copper Wire}
{artist: The Night Ferries}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Copper wire acro[F]ss the yard
[C]Humming like a slee[G]ping guard
[Am]Every bird that l[F]ands on it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[C]Sings a song and t[G]hen it quits
[Am]Sings a song an[F]d flies away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus (play loud)}
[F]Spark, spark[C], copper wire
[G]Carry me a litt[Am]le higher
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Hold the lin[C]e and hold it tight
[G]Bring the voice[Am]s home tonight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Harmonies}
[F]Ooh, copper wir[C]e, ooh
[G]Ooh, carry me h[Am]igher
{end_of_verse}
